    "body": "> Can we do this asynchronously with a timeout? Even if the syscall continues to run in the background?\r\n\r\nNot in 100% of the cases, but in your case, it might be possible. I originally thought that all remote syscalls might be unkillable for Samba, but thinking about it some more, that doesn't really make sense. So adding async sounds like one way to interrupt a misbehaving syscall.",
